==English==
{{was wotd|2007|October|1}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|name|sake}}. From the phrase "(one's) [[name]]'s [[sake]]"; first recorded in the mid-seventeenth century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|nāmʹsāk}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈneɪmseɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-namesake.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-namesake.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally}} One who is [[name]]d after another or for whom another is named.
#: {{syn|en|eponym}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[ship]] or a [[building]] that is named after someone or something.
# A person with the same name as another.

